fan, temperature.

398
00:17:02,567 --> 00:17:03,767
清清楚楚，没得挑。
No argument.

399
00:17:03,767 --> 00:17:05,133
说实话，唯一稍微有点奇怪的，
In fact,
the only slightly odd bit

400
00:17:05,167 --> 00:17:07,567
就是点火钥匙得插在中控台这里。
is that the ignition key
goes up here on the dashboard.

401
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:09,000
但你猜怎么着？
But you know what?

402
00:17:09,033 --> 00:17:11,767
放在这儿还真挺合适。
It's a really
good place for it.

403
00:17:11,767 --> 00:17:13,500
整车里里外外透着一股宜家风，
There's a touch
of IKEA to all this,

404
00:17:13,533 --> 00:17:17,367
但让人欣慰的是，这可是行家亲手组装的。
but, reassuringly, an expert
has put it all together.

405
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:18,800
他们甚至还玩了点泰特现代艺术馆的调调。
They've even gone
a bit Tate Modern.

406
00:17:18,833 --> 00:17:20,967
比如瞧瞧这个中控台。
Look at this centre console,
for example.

407
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:25,400
它不仅跟悬浮在外太空似的，
还是个镂空悬浮设计。
Not only is it
floating in outer space,
it's also see-through.

408
00:17:25,433 --> 00:17:27,033
可问题是，后面根本啥也看不到。
Except there isn't
anything to see.

409
00:17:27,067 --> 00:17:29,500
好歹让我瞅两眼电线布线什么的吧。
At least let me
look at some wiring
or something.

410
00:17:29,533 --> 00:17:31,167
验验焊接手艺也行啊。
Check the soldering.

411
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:33,867
我们现在已经不嘲笑沃尔沃旅行车车主了。
We don't laugh
at Volvo Estate drivers
any more.

412
00:17:33,900 --> 00:17:35,767
毕竟这种嘲讽现在都留给罗孚车主了。
We have Rover drivers
for that.

413
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:37,300
而我们笑不出来的原因之一，
And one of the reasons
we're not laughing

414
00:17:37,333 --> 00:17:41,067
就是眼前这种狠角色版本——T5。
is versions like
this one, the T5.

415
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:43,533
222匹马力。
222 horsepower.

416
00:17:43,567 --> 00:17:47,767
外加一颗涡轮增压器。
极速能飚到每小时150英里。
A turbo charger thrown in.
150 mph.

417
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:49,600
哎呦我的天！
Crivens!

418
00:17:51,767 --> 00:17:55,633
所以，座椅舒服、按键顺手、性能相当过得去。
So, comfy seats, nice buttons,
decent performance.

419
00:17:55,667 --> 00:17:57,467
开起来甚至还挺有乐趣。
It's even quite
good fun to drive.

420
00:17:57,500 --> 00:18:00,667
但在一辆沃尔沃旅行车上，
这些其实根本无关紧要。
But none of this
actually matters
in a Volvo Estate.

421
00:18:00,767 --> 00:18:04,067
真正重要的，是我到底能往后备厢里
What matters is
how big a piece of junk

422
00:18:04,100 --> 00:18:06,667
塞进多大一坨破烂。
I can fit in the back.

423
00:18:06,767 --> 00:18:09,300
沃尔沃以前的总设计师曾对我说过：
The old chief designer
of Volvo once told me that,

424
00:18:09,333 --> 00:18:11,133
“旅行车就是装了轮子的箱子。”
"Estates are boxes on wheels."

425
00:18:11,167 --> 00:18:13,333
它们生来就是拉货的，仅此而已。
They are for carrying stuff.
That's all there is to it.

426
00:18:13,367 --> 00:18:18,033
他还夸口说，沃尔沃造出了全天下最好的带轮大箱子。
And he said that Volvo made
the best boxes on wheels.

427
00:18:18,067 --> 00:18:21,967
呃，恐怕眼前这个箱子有点搞砸走形了。
Well, I'm afraid this box
has gone a bit pear-shaped.

428
00:18:24,500 --> 00:18:26,233
瞧瞧这个。
Have a look at this.

429
00:18:26,267 --> 00:18:29,467
这装载空间比宝马3系旅行版还要小，
That load space
is smaller than it is
on a BMW 3 Series Estate,

430
00:18:29,500 --> 00:18:34,067
不如奥迪A4旅行版，
甚至连捷豹新出的X-Type旅行版都干不过。
or an Audi A4 Estate,
or even the new
Jaguar X-type Estate.

431
00:18:34,100 --> 00:18:37,000
后排座椅立起时，
捷豹比它大概多了30升，
The Jaguar's got
about 30 litres more
with the seats up

432
00:18:37,033 --> 00:18:39,333
我估摸着大概也就这么大吧。
which I reckon
is probably about that much.

433
00:18:39,367 --> 00:18:42,500
但要是把后排一放倒，捷豹直接多出了100升。
But with the seats down,
it's got 100 litres more.

434
00:18:42,533 --> 00:18:44,900
那空间大概足够塞下……我也不知道，
And that's probably
enough for,
I don't know,

435
00:18:44,933 --> 00:18:48,133
比如一个雅致的维多利亚式毛毯木箱什么的。
a charming Victorian
blanket box or something.

436
00:18:49,633 --> 00:18:51,300
讲真，这可有点说不过去了，
Now, that's not
really good enough

437
00:18:51,333 --> 00:18:54,967
因为大空间本该是一辆沃尔沃旅行车的立身之本啊。
because space
is what a Volvo Estate
is supposed to be about.

438
00:18:55,633 --> 00:18:57,067
我说，这到底搞什么鬼？
I mean, what's going on?

439
00:19:00,067 --> 00:19:03,567
咱们到了，纽瓦克国际古董收藏品博览会，
Here we are, the Newark
International Antiques
and Collectors Fair,

440
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:05,000
就在诺丁汉郡。
in Nottinghamshire.

441
00:19:05,033 --> 00:19:06,800
这里是全欧洲最大的古董集市。
This is the biggest
antiques fair in Europe.

442
00:19:06,833 --> 00:19:10,567
要是我能在这儿淘到一件
足够有品位且块头够大的玩意儿，
If I can find something
suitably tasteful
and big here,

443
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:13,100
也许这辆沃尔沃
就能为自己挽回颜面了。
maybe the Volvo
can redeem itself.

444
00:19:14,833 --> 00:19:17,867
不过首先，
我得找个行家帮帮忙。
First though,
I'm going to need some help.

445
00:19:17,900 --> 00:19:20,367
这位是蒂姆·旺纳科特，
《寻宝探秘》节目的主持人。
This is Tim Wonnacott.
He's from Bargain Hunt.

446
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:22,167
- 欢迎来到《Top Gear》。
- 谢谢。
-Welcome to Top Gear.
-Thank you.

447
00:19:22,200 --> 00:19:24,933
他要帮我们以合理的价格，
淘到一件既体面又有品位的好东西。
And he's gonna help us
find something tasteful
at a reasonable price.

448
00:19:24,967 --> 00:19:26,300
看这样子，你已经有发现了？
I think, you've found
something already?

449
00:19:26,333 --> 00:19:28,000
确实有了，
你好好掌掌眼。
I have indeed.
Take this on board.

450
00:19:28,033 --> 00:19:32,300
纯银打造的。
维多利亚晚期到
爱德华时期的钟表，
It's solid silver.
A little late Victorian
Edwardian timepiece,

451
00:19:32,333 --> 00:19:35,400
铰链门保存完好，
机芯也相当不错……
all complete
with its hinge door,
nice movement...

452
00:19:35,433 --> 00:19:37,400
- 我能打断你一下吗？
- 请讲。
-Can I just stop
you there?
-Yeah.

453
00:19:37,433 --> 00:19:38,767
这玩意儿实在太小了。
It's not really big enough.

454
00:19:40,133 --> 00:19:43,667
我其实对什么年代或者岁月包浆毫无兴趣，
I'm not really interested
in period or patina,

455
00:19:43,767 --> 00:19:46,067
也不想要什么陶瓷娃娃，甚至老旧螺旋桨。
or porcelain dolls
or even an old propeller.

456
00:19:46,100 --> 00:19:48,200
我只想要一件能彻彻底底
I just want something
that will completely

457
00:19:48,233 --> 00:19:49,900
塞满我这辆沃尔沃后备厢的大家伙。
fill my Volvo's boot.

458
00:19:49,933 --> 00:19:51,000
……外框。
...frame.

459
00:19:51,033 --> 00:19:53,567
- 噢，等等。
- 怎么了？
-Oh, hang on.
-What?

460
00:19:53,600 --> 00:19:56,067
- 弹珠机！
- 你在逗我吧？
-Pinball.
-You are joking,
aren't you?

461
00:19:58,967 --> 00:20:01,333
这里绝大部分东西是不是纯粹的破烂？
Is the vast majority of it
complete tat?

462
00:20:01,367 --> 00:20:02,867
- 确实，瞧那个。
- 我挺喜欢那个的。
-Yeah, look at that.
-I like that.

463
00:20:02,900 --> 00:20:05,133
- 你喜欢？
- 是啊，我家就有一个类似的。
-You do?
-Yeah. I've got something
similar at home.

464
00:20:05,167 --> 00:20:06,667
这破玩意儿顶多值十镑！
It's £10's worth!

465
00:20:06,700 --> 00:20:08,600
管他呢，我可能还是会拿下。
Well, I might have it anyway.

466
00:20:08,633 --> 00:20:11,200
- 哎，这个倒是挺对我的胃口。
- 是吗？
-Now, I like the idea
of that.
-Do you?

467
00:20:11,233 --> 00:20:12,633
- 随时能搬走。
- 长蛀虫了吗？
-It's ready to go.
-Is it wormy?

468
00:20:12,667 --> 00:20:13,967
马上就能归你。
It could be yours.

469
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:15,400
- 不好说。
-（轻笑）没说你。
-Not sure.
-(CHUCKLES) Not you.

470
00:20:15,433 --> 00:20:16,867
- 漂亮！
- 什么？
-Yes!
-What?

471
00:20:16,900 --> 00:20:20,267
对！这简直太有《Top Gear》范儿了。
快看那个。
Yes. That is very Top Gear.
Look at that.

472
00:20:21,033 --> 00:20:22,767
算是皮质的吧，大概是。
It's leather, sort of.

473
00:20:22,800 --> 00:20:25,833
拉扣靠背，妥妥的绅士范儿。
It's button-backed.
It's gentlemanly.

474
00:20:25,867 --> 00:20:28,667
（吸鼻子）闻起来还有股老罗孚的味道。
(SNIFFS) And it smells
like an old Rover.

475
00:20:28,700 --> 00:20:30,600
这具漂亮的切斯特菲尔德沙发，
This beautiful Chesterfield

476
00:20:30,633 --> 00:20:33,133
塞进咱们这台瑞典旅行车里正合适。
should fit nicely
in our Swedish Estate.

477
00:20:33,167 --> 00:20:36,367
我是没看出这东西品质好在哪儿，
但要是你真喜欢的话……
Not sure where the quality is
there, but if you like it...

478
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:38,833
- 我爱死它了。多少钱？
- 蒂姆：你认真的？
-I love it. How much?
-TIM: You do?

479
00:20:38,867 --> 00:20:41,133
呃，看在你的面子上，
算你70镑吧。
Erm, I can do it
for you for £70.

480
00:20:41,167 --> 00:20:42,467
蒂姆：50镑怎么样？
TIM: What about £50?

481
00:20:42,500 --> 00:20:43,700
男人：少于70镑免谈。
MAN: £70, it's gotta be.

482
00:20:43,733 --> 00:20:46,667
50镑，别这样嘛。
50镑我就直接搬走了。
£50, come on.
Carry it away for £50.

483
00:20:46,700 --> 00:20:47,800
60镑，归你了。
£60, it's yours.

484
00:20:47,833 --> 00:20:49,867
60镑？那50镑怎么样？
£60, but what about 50?

485
00:20:49,900 --> 00:20:51,333
蒂姆：
各退一步，55镑。
TIM:
Split the difference, £55.

486
00:20:51,367 --> 00:20:52,600
55镑，成交。
£55, you got a deal.

487
00:20:52,633 --> 00:20:55,633
要是能塞进车里，
就算成交，行吧？
If it'll fit in the car,
then it's a deal, yeah?

488
00:20:55,667 --> 00:20:58,100
-行。
-成交，好嘞。
行，搬过来吧。
-Right.
-Done. Right.
Okay, bring it round.

489
00:20:59,433 --> 00:21:01,633
梅：
现在到了见证真相的时刻了。
MAY:
Now for the moment of truth.

490
00:21:01,667 --> 00:21:04,000
-（哼哧）
-蒂姆：往你那边推。
-(GRUNTS)
-TIM: To you.

491
00:21:04,033 --> 00:21:05,233
（蒂姆轻笑）
(TIM CHUCKLES)

492
00:21:05,267 --> 00:21:06,967
这人造革滑得我
手直打出溜。
My hands are slipping
on the leatherette.

493
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:09,867
-（蒂姆哼哧）
-你可能得把坐垫
稍微翘起来一点。
-(TIM GRUNTS)
-You might have to tip
the cushions a bit.

494
00:21:11,533 --> 00:21:13,633
（哼哧）加把劲，
往里推一把！
(GRUNTS) Go on,
give it a push!

495
00:21:13,667 --> 00:21:16,100
-（吃力）进去了！噢！
-太棒了。
-(STRAINED) Yes! Oh!
-Fantastic.

496
00:21:17,033 --> 00:21:18,267
等会儿。
Hang on.

497
00:21:20,233 --> 00:21:21,967
-不行。
-顶到底了吗？
-No.
-Is that at the end?

498
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:25,500
-蒂姆：到底了。
-哎，老天爷啊。
-TIM: Yeah.
-Oh, for Pete's sake.

499
00:21:25,533 --> 00:21:28,533
这要是捷豹或者奥迪，
早就装进去了。
That would have gone
in a Jag or an Audi.

500
00:21:31,133 --> 00:21:33,100
-你瞧，你自己看。
-噢！
-Look, just look.
-Oh!

501
00:21:33,133 --> 00:21:36,267
算了吧伙计，
根本塞不进去。
（轻笑）
Just forget it, mate.
It isn't gonna fit.
(CHUCKLES)

502
00:21:36,300 --> 00:21:39,100
那么詹姆斯，
你买了什么宝贝
来给我们演播室增光添彩啊？
So then, James,
what did you buy
to brighten up our studio?

503
00:21:39,133 --> 00:21:42,433
-你们准备好了吗？
-哈蒙德：准备好了，亮出来吧。
-Are you ready?
-HAMMOND: Yes, go on.

504
00:21:42,467 --> 00:21:44,533
-梅：瞧瞧这个怎么样？
-哈蒙德：哇哦！
-MAY: How about that?
-HAMMOND: Wow!

505
00:21:44,567 --> 00:21:46,767
这也太……
这也太棒了！
That's fan...
That's fantastic!

506
00:21:46,767 --> 00:21:48,667
-这是……
-梅：我当时就想到你了……
-It's...
-MAY: I was thinking of you...

507
00:21:48,767 --> 00:21:50,200
我每天都能
换个不同的发型……
I'm can have
a different hairstyle every...

508
00:21:50,233 --> 00:21:51,300
其实，
我有个更好的主意。
Actually,
I've had a better idea.

509
00:21:51,333 --> 00:21:52,500
刚才那个做头发的哥们儿呢？
Where's that hair bloke
earlier on?

510
00:21:52,533 --> 00:21:53,933
-哪儿？理发的。
-他在那边。
-Where? Hair.
-He's over there.

511
00:21:53,967 --> 00:21:55,767
过来！快过来！
快点！快过来！穿过来！
Come here! Come on!
Come on! Quick! Come through!

512
00:21:55,800 --> 00:21:58,333
跑快点！快来！
让让，借过借过！
快！快！快！
Come fast! Come on!
Make way, make way, make way!
Quick! Quick! Quick!

513
00:21:58,367 --> 00:21:59,533
赶紧的！伙计，
坐进去。
Come on! Get yourself
in there, mate.

514
00:21:59,567 --> 00:22:01,367
瞧，就是这儿！
Look, this is it!

515
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:03,067
坐下。
Sit.

516
00:22:03,100 --> 00:22:04,300
哇！瞧瞧这个！
Aw! Look at that!

517
00:22:04,333 --> 00:22:06,567
-我们把那个放那下面。
-（刺耳吱嘎声）
-We'll put that down there.
-(SCREECHING)

518
00:22:07,533 --> 00:22:09,000
对不住啊伙计。
Sorry, mate.

519
00:22:09,033 --> 00:22:11,867
你介意我们
先聊会儿车吗？
Do you mind
if we just discuss
the car momentarily?

520
00:22:11,900 --> 00:22:13,433
因为我前几天
刚开过这车。
'Cause I drove
one of these ones
the other day.

521
00:22:13,467 --> 00:22:16,333
-那是一辆柴油版的，
懂吗？我觉得……
-嗯。
-It was a diesel version,
okay? And I thought...
-Hmm.

522
00:22:16,367 --> 00:22:18,967
开起来有点单薄，
有点绵软无力。
It was a bit thin,
a bit weedy.

523
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:21,467
其实你说得没错。
因为那台T5
开起来还挺有意思的，
You're right, actually.
Because that T5
is quite good fun,

524
00:22:21,500 --> 00:22:24,900
-但老实说，同车系剩下的型号
都挺无聊的。
-克拉克森：对。
-but the rest of the range
is a bit boring, to be honest.
-CLARKSON: Yeah.

525
00:22:24,933 --> 00:22:27,033
而且你上周开的那辆捷豹，
And the Jag
that you had last week,

526
00:22:27,067 --> 00:22:29,500
-那辆X-Type，X-Type旅行版……
-对。
-the X-type, X-type Estate...
-Yeah.

527
00:22:29,533 --> 00:22:31,467
……显然要实用得多。
...is more practical,
obviously.

528
00:22:31,500 --> 00:22:33,833
呃，发动机更好，
开起来也更有乐趣。
Uh, it's got a nicer engine.
It's more fun to drive.

529
00:22:33,867 --> 00:22:36,000
而且说实话，它俩价格
基本差不多。
And actually, it costs
pretty much the same money.

530
00:22:36,033 --> 00:22:37,833
你要是开那辆X-Type去，
And if you'd taken
the X-type up there,

531
00:22:37,867 --> 00:22:40,067
我们就能把那个绿沙发
搬回来了，
we could have had
that green sofa,

532
00:22:40,100 --> 00:22:42,967
-你也不至于
被羞辱得这么惨。
-没错。
-and you wouldn't
have been humiliated so much.
-Yeah.

533
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:45,600
捷豹居然造出了
比沃尔沃更好的旅行车。
Jaguar's built
a better estate than Volvo.

534
00:22:45,633 --> 00:22:47,867
-这说明了什么？
-不知道，太邪门了。
-What does that mean?
-I don't know. Weird.

535
00:22:47,900 --> 00:22:50,533
行了，言归正传，
是时候见见我们的嘉宾了。
Anyway. We've got
to move on. It's time
