It's not the usual American
enormous saloon

1075
00:51:29,200 --> 00:51:31,400
机舱里硬塞一台
从战列舰上拆下来的发动机。
with the engine
out of a battleship.

1076
00:51:31,433 --> 00:51:35,067
这辆车打一开始，
就是纯粹作为跑车而打造的。
This has always been
purpose built as a sports car.

1077
00:51:35,100 --> 00:51:38,167
而且半个世纪以来，
它的祖传配方从未变过：
And in half a century,
the recipe has never changed.

1078
00:51:38,200 --> 00:51:43,700
永远是流线型车身、
永远是后驱、
永远是玻璃纤维车壳。
Always a sweeping body,
always rear drive,
always fibreglass.

1079
00:51:43,733 --> 00:51:46,967
所以，
这就是美国的保时捷911。
This then,
is America's Porsche 911.

1080
00:51:47,000 --> 00:51:53,133
但在我们欧洲，早就有一辆保时捷911了。
它的名字就叫保时捷911。
But here in Europe, we already
have a Porsche 911.
It's called the Porsche 911.

1081
00:51:53,167 --> 00:51:56,167
所以我们向来对克尔维特
没多大兴趣。
So we've never been
too interested in the 'Vette.

1082
00:51:58,833 --> 00:52:02,933
但这可拦不住美国佬
硬想把这玩意儿兜售给我们。
But that's not gonna put off
the Americans from trying
to sell them to us.

1083
00:52:02,967 --> 00:52:07,400
买一辆丐版保时捷911
得花你六万英镑，
And whilst a basic 911
will set you back £60,000,

1084
00:52:07,433 --> 00:52:10,533
而这台只要更亲民的
四万英镑。
this costs a more modest
£40,000.

1085
00:52:11,900 --> 00:52:15,767
掏这点钱，你就能买到一台
400匹马力的6.0升V8发动机。
For that, you get a six-litre
V8 with 400 bhp.

1086
00:52:15,800 --> 00:52:19,400
但更重要的是，
足足400磅-英尺的扭矩。
But more importantly,
400lb-ft of torque.

1087
00:52:19,433 --> 00:52:25,500
这力道足够把那边所有的树全连根拔起，
然后再狠狠栽到另一边去。
Now that's enough to pull up
all of those trees over there
and put them over there.

1088
00:52:25,533 --> 00:52:28,367
就冲这价格，
听着简直像是捡了大便宜。
Now for the price,
that may seem like a bargain.

1089
00:52:28,400 --> 00:52:33,000
但悲催的是，这车上
也到处都是廉价处理品的质感。
But sadly, there's also
quite a lot of this car
that's bargain basement.

1090
00:52:33,033 --> 00:52:36,933
（塑料敲击声）这塑料件，
他们到底是从哪儿搞来的？
(CLANKING) These plastics,
where are they
getting them from?

1091
00:52:36,967 --> 00:52:39,533
我们开过的每一辆美国车
全都是这副德行。
It's the same
with every American car
we drive.

1092
00:52:39,567 --> 00:52:42,867
这帮人可是能把人送上火星的啊！
These are the people
that can land on Mars!

1093
00:52:42,900 --> 00:52:46,767
而且一旦开起来，
更遭罪的还在后头。
And there's more misery
to come
when you're driving it.

1094
00:52:46,800 --> 00:52:48,867
这离合踩得
我左腿生疼。
The clutch is making
my left leg hurt.

1095
00:52:48,900 --> 00:52:52,400
换挡手感简直就像
直接从维多利亚时期的铁路信号房里拆出来的。
And the gear change
has been taken straight out
of a Victorian signal box.

1096
00:52:52,433 --> 00:52:54,133
（呼气）我换个挡啊。
(EXHALES) I'm changing gear.

1097
00:52:54,167 --> 00:52:55,567
（痛苦呻吟）
(GROANS)

1098
00:52:56,967 --> 00:52:59,067
接下来是底盘技术。
And then there's the
chassis technology.

1099
00:52:59,100 --> 00:53:02,500
克尔维特的后悬挂
居然用的是钢板弹簧。
The Corvette's rear suspension
uses leaf springs.

1100
00:53:03,733 --> 00:53:06,367
我给你们打个生动的比方。
Let me make that live for you.

1101
00:53:06,400 --> 00:53:12,833
要是你去看医生，
结果他掏出一罐水蛭要给你放血，你懂我意思了吧。
If you went to your doctor's,
and he got a jar of leeches
out, you know what I mean.

1102
00:53:12,867 --> 00:53:14,467
这还没完呢。
And I haven't finished yet.

1103
00:53:14,500 --> 00:53:15,933
还有它的乘坐质感。
There's still the ride.

1104
00:53:17,667 --> 00:53:20,133
我来让你们切身感受一下
这到底意味着什么。
Let me show you
exactly what that means.

1105
00:53:23,100 --> 00:53:24,433
走起。
Here we go.

1106
00:53:24,467 --> 00:53:26,100
（颠得叫苦）哎哟！
(GROANING) Ooh!

1107
00:53:26,133 --> 00:53:29,833
天哪。这就是美国跑车图腾的
巅峰之作？
Oh, dear. Is this the pinnacle
of American sports car icons?

1108
00:53:29,867 --> 00:53:33,133
一个内饰奇烂、换挡死沉的
塑料大楔子，
A plastic wedge
with a horrible interior,
clunky transmission

1109
00:53:33,167 --> 00:53:36,500
悬挂技术还是直接从《圣经·旧约》里刨出来的。
and suspension technology
lifted from the Old Testament.

1110
00:53:36,533 --> 00:53:41,467
好吧，但愿克尔维特能靠纯正的老派蛮力
挽回点颜面。
Well, let's hope the Corvette
can redeem itself
with good old-fashioned grunt.

1111
00:53:46,367 --> 00:53:50,933
这向来是美国跑车的
看家绝活。
Now this has always been
the party piece
of the American sports car.

1112
00:53:50,967 --> 00:53:53,833
那么这家伙能否秉承
他们政府的一贯传统，
So can this one follow
in the tradition
of its government

1113
00:53:53,867 --> 00:53:55,967
四处去给其他国家
添堵呢？
and get up
other countries' noses?

1114
00:53:58,267 --> 00:54:01,267
我们今天搞的是一场“联合国直线加速赛”，
What we've got here
is a United Nations drag race

1115
00:54:01,300 --> 00:54:06,567
英国代表队出战的是
350匹马力的TVR 350。
with Britain being represented
by a 350bhp TVR 350.

1116
00:54:06,667 --> 00:54:09,200
日本代表是本田NSX。
Japan by the Honda NSX.

1117
00:54:09,233 --> 00:54:11,433
德国代表则是一辆911。
And from Germany, a 911.

1118
00:54:11,467 --> 00:54:13,967
（引擎轰鸣）
(ENGINES REVVING)

1119
00:54:16,033 --> 00:54:19,933
大家的马力都大差不差，
全都是专门为干这行而生的纯种机器。
All with roughly
the same power,
all purpose built for the job.

1120
00:54:21,500 --> 00:54:23,200
好了，起步有点打滑。
Okay, bit of
spin off the line.

1121
00:54:25,400 --> 00:54:26,800
保时捷
简直是在倒退。
The Porsche
has gone backwards.

1122
00:54:26,833 --> 00:54:30,567
TVR一路绝尘，
势不可挡。
The TVR is
absolutely steaming ahead.

1123
00:54:31,667 --> 00:54:34,067
跟那台日本车NSX
并驾齐驱。
Neck and neck with the NSX,
the Japanese.

1124
00:54:35,000 --> 00:54:36,500
噢，这下可难看了。
Oh, this looks poor.

1125
00:54:36,533 --> 00:54:38,667
克尔维特
惨兮兮地落到了第三。
A lowly third
for the Corvette.

1126
00:54:38,667 --> 00:54:41,000
英国队！哎呀，他们赢了。
The Brits! Oh, dear, they win.

1127
00:54:42,533 --> 00:54:46,100
那么，这美国货
到底有没有擅长的事？
So, is this American any good
at anything?

1128
00:54:46,133 --> 00:54:47,933
其实，还真有。
Well, actually, yes.

1129
00:54:49,233 --> 00:54:52,300
抬头显示，
这玩意儿很酷。
The head-up display,
that's cool.

1130
00:54:52,333 --> 00:54:53,900
这绝对是个好东西。
That's a very good thing.

1131
00:54:53,933 --> 00:54:58,667
能显示转速、车速
还有各种信息，
相当管用。
It shows you revs and
speed and all sorts,
which is useful.

1132
00:54:58,667 --> 00:55:01,367
还有这个，
挺有意思。
And here's something else.
Interesting.

1133
00:55:01,400 --> 00:55:03,233
一个G值表。
A G-metre.

1134
00:55:03,267 --> 00:55:05,500
可一台美国车
Now, why would an American car

1135
00:55:06,167 --> 00:55:07,667
要G值表干嘛？
need a G-metre?

1136
00:55:07,700 --> 00:55:09,433
给你个线索。
Well, here's a clue.

1137
00:55:09,467 --> 00:55:12,133
新款克尔维特比老款
短了整整5英寸。
The new Corvette
is 5 inches shorter
than the old one.

1138
00:55:12,167 --> 00:55:15,000
而且车轮更贴近车身四角。
And the wheels are closer
to the ends of the car.

1139
00:55:15,033 --> 00:55:17,667
他们这么做只有一个原因。
And there's only one reason
they did that.

1140
00:55:17,700 --> 00:55:20,667
就是为了让它过弯更利落。
To make it better
at going round corners.

1141
00:55:21,567 --> 00:55:22,833
（轮胎尖叫声）
(TYRES SCREECHING)

1142
00:55:31,033 --> 00:55:34,300
车身感觉很小巧，
开起来很灵活。
It feels small,
it feels nimble.

1143
00:55:34,333 --> 00:55:37,400
转向听话，
入弯极其利落。
It's steerable,
it turns in quickly.

1144
00:55:37,433 --> 00:55:39,133
太神了。
看，前面是个弯道。
This is amazing.
Look, this is a corner.

1145
00:55:39,167 --> 00:55:41,100
我们顺畅拐过来了！
We go round a bend.

1146
00:55:41,133 --> 00:55:44,267
美国哪有这玩意儿啊。
他们打哪儿学会这手艺的？
They don't have these
in America. How do they know
how to do this?

1147
00:55:44,300 --> 00:55:49,567
虽然底下用的只是钢板弹簧，
但查尔顿·赫斯顿开的双轮战车也是啊。
It may only have leaf springs
underneath, but so did
Charlton Heston's chariot.

1148
00:55:49,667 --> 00:55:51,133
可瞧瞧人家玩得多痛快！
And look at the fun he had.

1149
00:55:53,300 --> 00:55:58,567
当你狠狠踩下油门时，
它的声浪听起来
就像台地道的肌肉车了。
And when you really hammer it,
it starts to sound
like a proper muscle car.

1150
00:55:59,433 --> 00:56:00,867
（引擎咆哮）
(ENGINE ROARS)

1151
00:56:04,767 --> 00:56:08,933
话说回来，每次我们测前殖民地的车，
好像都是一个德行。
You know this seems to happen
every time we test a car
from the colonies.

1152
00:56:08,967 --> 00:56:12,067
杰里米开那台澳大利亚霍顿的时候，
也是这副模样。
It was the same when Jeremy
drove that Australian Holden.

1153
00:56:12,100 --> 00:56:15,733
做工是糙了点，
但确实是实打实的好玩，爽翻天。
They're a bit crude,
but really, really big fun.

1154
00:56:18,400 --> 00:56:20,500
这台车就像个美式橄榄球运动员。
This one is like
an American footballer.

1155
00:56:20,533 --> 00:56:23,667
看着可能头脑简单，
甚至会在体育酒吧里狂打响嗝。
It might look simple.
It might belch in sports bars.

1156
00:56:23,667 --> 00:56:26,033
但在那副皮囊之下，
它绝对是个优秀的运动健将。
But underneath,
there's quite an athlete.

1157
00:56:28,767 --> 00:56:32,733
我能给你们看个东西吗？
介意我给你们瞅一眼吗？看这个。
Can I just show you something?
Do you mind if I just show you
something? Look at this.

1158
00:56:32,767 --> 00:56:34,300
-知道啦，我知道！
-看那玩意儿！
-Yes, I know!
-Look at that!

1159
00:56:34,333 --> 00:56:35,667
-是啊，我知道。
-瞧瞧它。
-Yeah, I know.
-Look at it.

1160
00:56:35,700 --> 00:56:37,667
要是你是个倒霉的路人，
这车倒车把你撞上了……
If you're a pedestrian,
and this backs into you,

1161
00:56:37,667 --> 00:56:39,133
那你肯定会为此
感到庆幸的。
you'd be very pleased
for that.

1162
00:56:39,167 --> 00:56:40,467
挺舒服的。
It's comfy.

1163
00:56:40,500 --> 00:56:42,833
我能不能再提一下
刚才片子里的另一件事？
And can I just bring
something else up
from the film?

1164
00:56:42,867 --> 00:56:43,933
说吧。
Yes.

1165
00:56:43,967 --> 00:56:45,233
-钢板弹簧。
-噢。
-Leaf springs.
-Oh.

1166
00:56:45,267 --> 00:56:47,300
是啊，嗯……
虽然原始，但挺管用啊。
Yes, well,
basic but functional.

1167
00:56:47,333 --> 00:56:48,800
-钢板弹簧啊！
-是，我……
-Leaf springs!
-Yeah, I...

1168
00:56:48,833 --> 00:56:51,667
那玩意儿只有
银十字牌婴儿车上才用！
Like you get
on a Silver Cross pram.

1169
00:56:51,667 --> 00:56:53,533
-没错！
-或者中世纪牛车！
-Yes!
-Or a medieval ox cart.

1170
00:56:53,567 --> 00:56:55,733
确实，但它真顶用！
This is true, but they work!

1171
00:56:56,167 --> 00:56:58,067
你总不会……
You're not

1172
00:56:58,100 --> 00:57:02,767
真的以为这台车
跑赛道能有……比如，
seriously suggesting that
this car could go round
the track as fast as, say,

1173
00:57:02,800 --> 00:57:04,567
俄罗斯造的TVR那么快吧？
a Russian TVR?

1174
00:57:04,667 --> 00:57:09,667
测测就知道。是时候
跟“乔治·W·斯提格”
来一场“震慑行动”了！
Let's find out. It's time
for some shock and awe
with George W Stig.

1175
00:57:09,667 --> 00:57:11,933
起跑了！
起步疯狂打滑！
And away he goes.
Loads of wheel spin
off the line.

1176
00:57:11,967 --> 00:57:15,900
别忘了那可是足足400匹
狂暴怒吼的西部烈马
在奋力反抗。
Don't forget that's
400 snarling Wild West horses
fighting back.

1177
00:57:15,933 --> 00:57:18,433
问题是过弯的时候
它们会不会让人日子不好过？
Question is will they
make life difficult
through the corners?

1178
00:57:18,467 --> 00:57:19,867
甩尾了！
There's oversteering there!

1179
00:57:19,900 --> 00:57:22,333
严重的转向过度，
这可有点让人捏把汗了。
A lot of oversteer,
which is a bit of a worry.

1180
00:57:22,367 --> 00:57:23,667
瞧瞧那姿态。
Look at that.

1181
00:57:24,667 --> 00:57:26,833
（摇滚乐响起）
(ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)

1182
00:57:32,167 --> 00:57:34,533
噢！进芝加哥弯的时候
前轮直接抱死了！
Oh! Locking the front wheels
into Chicago there!

1183
00:57:34,567 --> 00:57:38,700
开克尔维特重刹的时候，
车尾确实会变得很不老实。
It does get a bit frisky
when you're braking
very hard on the Corvette.

1184
00:57:38,733 --> 00:57:40,167
现在切入锤头弯。
Coming around
to the Hammerhead now.

1185
00:57:40,200 --> 00:57:41,800
很多车在这里都会推头。
Lots of cars understeer here.

1186
00:57:42,667 --> 00:57:44,667
但这台不会。
But not this one.

1187
00:57:44,700 --> 00:57:47,000
你甚至能听出斯提格在那里
轻点油门试探，
You can actually hear
The Stig feathering
the accelerator around there,

1188
00:57:47,033 --> 00:57:49,167
极力想把躁动的车尾
按在行车线上。
trying to keep
that back end in line.

1189
00:57:52,067 --> 00:57:54,133
他现在正全速冲向贯通弯。
He's heading up towards
the follow through now.

1190
00:57:54,167 --> 00:57:56,033
按说克尔维特在这里
应该极快。
Now, the Corvette should be
very fast here.

1191
00:57:56,067 --> 00:57:58,200
斯提格终于能彻底释放
那台大V8的威力了。
The Stig can really
open up that big V8.

1192
00:57:59,467 --> 00:58:01,600
噢！这速度可真够猛的！
Ooh! That is properly quick!

1193
00:58:01,633 --> 00:58:04,800
前半圈里，这台雪佛兰
眼看就要跑出一个相当稳健的圈速。
Now in the first half
of the lap, the Chevy was
looking set for a solid time.

1194
00:58:04,833 --> 00:58:06,433
本来很有可能
跑进1分28、29秒左右。
It could have been
in the high 1.20s.

1195
00:58:06,467 --> 00:58:07,967
他能稳住吗？
Will he hold on to that?

1196
00:58:08,000 --> 00:58:10,133
刚才那下有点走形了。
Bit messy there.

1197
00:58:10,167 --> 00:58:13,100
逼近甘邦弯，过弯又甩尾了！
冲线成绩是……
Coming towards Gambon,
more oversteer through there!
And across the line in...

1198
00:58:13,867 --> 00:58:15,300
-是多少？
-1分……
-In what?
-One...

1199
00:58:15,333 --> 00:58:17,933
-排在这下面，对。很明显……
-那还不错。对。20……
-Down here, yes. Obviously...
-Which is good. Yes. 20...

1200
00:58:18,700 --> 00:58:21,367
6秒8！
6.8!

1201
00:58:21,400 --> 00:58:25,233
这车是真快啊！
对不住了克拉克森，
你没法不认账，你瞧瞧！
Now that is a fast car!
I'm sorry! You can't deny it,
Clarkson. Look at that!

1202
00:58:25,267 --> 00:58:28,333
-确实不赖！
-比……我是说，
都快赶上Evo了！
-That's not bad!
-It's faster than... I mean,
it's nearly as fast as an Evo!

1203
00:58:28,367 --> 00:58:31,100
-梅：这车确实快。
-这点我认。
确实是非常快……
-MAY: It's a quick car.
-I'll grant you that.
It's a very quick...

1204
00:58:31,133 --> 00:58:33,200
虽然跑得乱七八糟，
但圈速相当惊人。
A messy lap,
but a very quick time.

1205
00:58:33,233 --> 00:58:38,467
所以结论在这儿了。如果你想要一辆
塑料壳、左舵、
还配着越南悬挂的车，
So there we are. If you want
a plastic left-hand drive car
with Vietnamese suspension,

1206
00:58:38,500 --> 00:58:40,700
-那就是它了。
-那也是真的快！
-here it is.
-That's very fast!

1207
00:58:40,733 --> 00:58:43,167
随便吧。不过很遗憾，
本期节目到这就结束了。
Whatever. That is the end
of the show, I'm afraid.

1208
00:58:43,200 --> 00:58:45,167
而且事实上，
本季节目也就此收官了。
And, in fact, the end
of the series.

1209
00:58:45,200 --> 00:58:46,600
我们秋天见。
So we'll see you
in the autumn.

1210
00:58:46,633 --> 00:58:48,033
非常感谢各位
收看本节目。
Thanks very much
for tuning in.

1211
00:58:48,067 --> 00:58:49,467
到时候见，晚安！
See you then. Good night!

